Z||000000||fiero56||04-20-2001||11:31 AM||||This has been going on for several weeks now, and before we take it to the dealership(for other warranty issues as well), wondering what could be causing this.<P>My folks have a 2000 Chrysler Town & Country LXi(LXi designation might make a difference since it has different electronics?) minivan they bought new 15 months ago. Evertime we have the headlights on(at night) the digital readouts for odometer, transmission selector, radio digital display, and overhead displays for direction, temp, etc, will periodically go blank for up to several seconds, and will eventually light up again. This never happens when the headlights are off, but the displays are still at the same illumination setting. Makes me think it could be with a swtich, but then why is it only the digital readouts and not the backlighting for the gages, and radio buttons and such? I just don't want a computer or something going out while on a trip, since only the digital stuff is affected.||||reg||5
